Description: nir/opt_vectorize_io: keep dual-source blend outputs apart
 Both colours of dual-source blending are stored at the same location
 (FRAG_RESULT_DATA0) and differ only in dual_source_blend_index.
 compare_is_not_vectorizable() did not look at the index, so after
 nir_lower_io_to_scalar() the scalar stores of both colours fell into one
 group, and vectorize_batch() removed the earlier store of each component as
 overwritten. With the shader order of the CTS (index 0 first) only the
 index 1 colour was left.
 .
 pco runs nir_lower_io_to_scalar(), nir_opt_cse() and nir_opt_vectorize_io()
 on fragment outputs before nir_lower_blend() (pco_lower_nir()). Once CSE
 has merged the zero offsets, nir_lower_blend() found only the second colour,
 took it as src1 in consume_dual_stores(), and the shader stored no colour at
 all. The index is now compared like the location, so both colours are
 vectorized separately.
 .
 Needed by 0054 (dualSrcBlend); without dual-source blending no shader has
 an output with index 1, so nothing changes there.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
